# Route guides maintenance

Whenever you **implement or materially change** a page, section, or feature in `apps/web`, update the matching guide under **`docs/guides/routes/`** in the **same change** — not as a follow-up.

## Which file to update

Mirror the app URL (omit dynamic params), rooted at `docs/guides/routes/`. Authoritative index: **`docs/guides/routes/README.md`** — do not maintain a second route→file table here.

Examples:

| Route pattern | Guide location |
| --- | --- |
| `/dashboard/patients/...` | `docs/guides/routes/dashboard/patients/...` |
| `/dashboard/appointments/...` | `docs/guides/routes/dashboard/appointments/...` |
| `/dashboard/patients/:id/visits/:visitId` | `docs/guides/routes/dashboard/patients/detail.md` (document dynamic params inline) |
| `/book/:clinicSlug` (public self-service booking) | `docs/guides/routes/book.md` |
| `/settings/...` | `docs/guides/routes/settings/...` |

## What to document

Per page/section: **behavior**, **save paths** (UI action → API endpoint → DB effect), **validation**, **RBAC** (which roles can view/edit), **AI assistant parity** (is there an equivalent assistant tool? if not, why not), **edge cases**, **implementation map** (web + API paths), and **Host-facing knowledge** (plain-language summary + common front-desk/doctor Q&A — no code, no DB column names, no internal endpoint names; written so the AI Clinic Assistant or a support person can quote it directly).

Update the **Progress overview** table when section status changes. Mark guide **Status** from `Pending` → `Documented` when substantive. Template: `docs/guides/_template.md`.

## When guides need no change

Typos, internal renames with no behavior change, or pure refactors that don't alter UX/API/validation.
